Keep a shared pool as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared candidate as empty text.
Keep a shared bestsub as empty text.
Keep a shared lefttext as empty text.
Keep a shared righttext as empty text.
Keep a shared mixed as empty text.
Keep a shared bestmixed as empty text.
Keep a shared overall as empty text.
Keep a shared picklo as 0.
Keep a shared pickhi as 0.
Keep a shared pickmask as 0.
Keep a shared started as 0.
Keep a shared improve as 0.
Keep a shared bestmask as 0.
Place 3 into pool.
Place 4 into pool.
Place 6 into pool.
Place 5 into pool.
Place 9 into pool.
Place 1 into pool.
Place 2 into pool.
Place 5 into pool.
Place 8 into pool.
Place 3 into pool.
To attach from spot (a whole number).
The digit is item spot of pool.
The symbol is the character for digit.
Place symbol into candidate.

To gather from spot (a whole number).
If spot is more than pickhi, return.
The offset is spot minus picklo.
The raised is shift 1 left by offset.
The bit is bitwise and of pickmask and raised.
If bit is more than 0, attach from spot.
Gather from spot plus 1.

To judge from spot (a whole number).
If bestsub comes before candidate, set improve to 1.

To pick from lo (a whole number) with hi (a whole number) and target (a whole number).
Set bestsub to empty text.
Set picklo to lo.
Set pickhi to hi.
Set started to 0.
If target is 0, return.
For every mask from 0 to 63.
Set pickmask to mask.
Set candidate to empty text.
Gather from picklo.
The lastp is the last position of candidate.
The length is lastp plus 1.
If length is target.
Set improve to 0.
If started is 0, set improve to 1.
If started is 1, judge from 0.
If improve is 1, Set bestsub to empty text, Place candidate into bestsub, set started to 1.

To leftstep from i (a whole number) with j (a whole number).
The piece is the slice of lefttext from i to i plus 1.
Place piece into mixed.
Blend from i plus 1 with j.
Remove last character from mixed.

To rightstep from i (a whole number) with j (a whole number).
The piece is the slice of righttext from j to j plus 1.
Place piece into mixed.
Blend from i with j plus 1.
Remove last character from mixed.

To score from spot (a whole number).
If started is 0, Set bestmixed to empty text, Place mixed into bestmixed, set started to 1, return.
If bestmixed comes before mixed, Set bestmixed to empty text, Place mixed into bestmixed.

To judgeover from spot (a whole number).
If overall comes before bestmixed, set improve to 1.

To blend from i (a whole number) with j (a whole number).
The leftlast is the last position of lefttext.
The rightlast is the last position of righttext.
If i is more than leftlast and j is more than rightlast, score from 0, return.
If i is at most leftlast, leftstep from i with j.
If j is at most rightlast, rightstep from i with j.

For every firstcount from 0 to 4.
The secondcount is 5 minus firstcount.
If secondcount is at most 6.
Set bestsub to empty text.
Pick from 0 with 3 and firstcount.
Set lefttext to empty text.
Place bestsub into lefttext.
Set bestsub to empty text.
Pick from 4 with 9 and secondcount.
Set righttext to empty text.
Place bestsub into righttext.
Set mixed to empty text.
Set bestmixed to empty text.
Set started to 0.
Blend from 0 with 0.
The oversize is the last position of overall.
Set improve to 0.
If oversize is -1, set improve to 1.
If improve is 0, judgeover from 0.
If improve is 1, Set overall to empty text, Place bestmixed into overall.

The line is empty text.
For every spot from 0 to 4.
If spot is more than 0, Place "," into line.
The piece is the slice of overall from spot to spot plus 1.
Place piece into line.

Show line.
